==English (BCEN)==
*The main currency used during [[Battle|battle]] is cents (¢).
*The game can be played in English, French, Italian, German, Spanish or Thai.
*The [[Into the Future]] menu button has a blue background and white name; in other versions, it has a blue name on a background with the same colors as the [[Empire of Cats]] and [[Cats of the Cosmos]] menu buttons.
*The exclusive anniversary stages are [[Faster Than Fast Food|Minced Meet-Up]] and [[Catburger Awakens!]], which drop [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]] and its [[True Form]] respectively.
*[[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Wind Dancer Valkyrie]] is clad in a Native American-style outfit while [[Li'l Valkyrie Dark (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Rider Valkyrie]] is dressed as a cowboy.
*In 2017, three of the [[Serial Codes|serial code]] units were brought back in events that never came to the other versions:
**The [[Cat Bros (Special Cat)|Cat Bros]] were received from the stage "[[We're Number One|For the Fans]]" from May 1st, 2017 to May 8th, 2017.
**[[Capsule Cat (Special Cat)|Capsule Cat]] was distributed as a stamp reward during the exclusive [[MattShea Collaboration Event|MattShea collab]].
**[[Squish Ball Cat (Special Cat)|Squish Ball Cat]] could be obtained from the stage "[[None More Squishy|Watch & Earn]]" from August 16th, 2017 to August 30th, 2017, during the [[PONOS Campaigns/Cats 'Round The World|Cats 'Round The World]] event.
*The [[Million Downloads Event/88.88 Million|88.88 Million Downloads Event]] was exclusive to BCEN.
*The winner of [[PONOS Campaigns/The OutCats|The OutCats]] campaign was [[Trash Cat (Special Cat)|Trash Cat]], obtained from the [[Catnip Challenges]] after beating [[Sender Unknown|Mystery Package]] during the 88.88M Downloads Worldwide Event.
*[[Road to Unification]] appeared as a standalone event from June 20th, 2025 to July 25th, 2025 rather than being part of the [[Anniversary/12th Year|12th Anniversary]].
*It is the only version to have not received the [[Gudetama Collaboration Event|Gudetama collab]].

==Taiwanese (BCTW)==
*The main currency used during [[Battle|battle]] is yuan (元).
*The first six stages of [[Empire of Cats]] are conquered in a different order and include two locations and enemy bases that aren't in the other versions. The order is Taiwan, Hong Kong, Thailand, China, Mongolia and Korea; [[Cambodia (Empire of Cats)|Cambodia]] and [[Philippines (Empire of Cats)|Philippines]] do not appear.
*[[Into the Future]] also features Taiwan and Hong Kong, as stages 3 and 21 respectively. The locations in between are all shifted forward by 1 (i.e., [[China (Into the Future)|China]] is stage 4 instead of 3), changing the names and enemy bases but not the backgrounds. [[Cambodia (Into the Future)|Cambodia]] and [[Philippines (Into the Future)|Philippines]] are again absent.
*The exclusive anniversary stage is [[Secret Delicacy|Baozi ★ Q Bomb Strikes]], which drops [[Baozi Cat (Special Cat)|Baozi Cat]].
*[[Crazed Baozi Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Baozi Cat]] is distributed as a stamp reward during anniversaries.
*[[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] does not have "NEKO" on its wrapper. The same also applies to [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]].
*[[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]]'s shirt says "I Love Fish" in English instead of "I Love さば" (''saba'', meaning "mackerel").
*[[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Cats in a Box]] do not have the "バナナ" (''banana'') text on their box, and likewise for the "みかん" (''mikan'', meaning "orange") on Cat Gang's.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]]'s fans have stars instead of "祭" (''matsuri'', meaning "festival").
*[[Sports Day Cat (Rare Cat)|Sports Day Cat]]'s headband is blue instead of red.
*[[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Wind Dancer Valkyrie]] and [[Li'l Valkyrie Dark (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Rider Valkyrie]] are clad in traditional Chinese-style outfits, the same as in BCJP.
*The winner of [[PONOS Campaigns/The OutCats|The OutCats]] campaign was [[Trash Cat (Special Cat)|Trash Cat]].
*There have been four exclusive collabs:
**[[Hiroshi Mihara Collaboration Event|Hiroshi Mihara]]
**[[Chocolate Collaboration Event|Chocolate]]
**[[Maji Island Tour Collaboration Event|Maji Island Tour]]
**[[Kaohsiung Rapid Transit Collaboration Event|Kaohsiung Rapid Transit]]
*It is one of the two versions to have received the [[Castle & Dragon Collaboration Event|Castle & Dragon]] collab, the other being BCJP.

==Korean (BCKR)==
*The main currency used during [[Battle|battle]] is won (원).
*The exclusive anniversary stages are [[Punchy Prizefighter|Korean Special Stage]] and [[Nekondo Awakens!]], which drop [[Nekondo (Special Cat)|Nekondo]] and its True Form respectively.
*Unit 182 is [[Cuckoo Crew 12 (Special Cat)|Cuckoo Crew 12]] (based on the Korean YouTuber [https://www.youtube.com/user/realcuckoocrew Cuckoo Crew]), which could be unlocked via [[Serial Codes|serial code]].
*The [[Joy & Prosperity|Lunar New Year]] stage has a different enemy base and background.
*[[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]]'s shirt says "I Love Fish" in English instead of "I Love さば" (''saba'', meaning "mackerel").
*[[Sports Day Cat (Rare Cat)|Sports Day Cat]]'s headband is blue instead of red.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]]'s fans have stars instead of "祭" (''matsuri'', meaning "festival").
*The winner of [[PONOS Campaigns/The OutCats|The OutCats]] campaign was [[Stealth Cat (Special Cat)|Stealth Cat]].
*The song "[https://youtu.be/Mqps4anhz0Q Senbonzakura]" is omitted from all [[Hatsune Miku Collaboration Event]] stages, replaced by other songs featured in the collab.

